# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters: size, and secrets. The
# build context is uploaded to the daemon and every COPY reads from it, so a
# stray `.env` here is a database password inside an image layer.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.husky

node_modules
.next
out
build

# Generated at build time by `pnpm db:generate`. Copying a host-built client in
# would overwrite it with one compiled for the wrong platform.
lib/generated

backups
*.log

# Documentation and source material. None of it is read at runtime, and
# edu-reference alone is tens of megabytes of the university's own files.
docs
documentation
edu-reference
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling and editor state
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.playwright-mcp
coverage
*.png
!public/**/*.png

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
